            </note>
            <note corresp="#d38-f2" n="1" xml:id="d38-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d38-f3" n="2" xml:id="d38-f3-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated to Tehran, Cairo, London, and Baghdad. Ambassador
                    Childs reviewed the situation with the Saudi Arabian Foreign Office in the light
                    of telegram 190. He emphasized “again danger of delay, advantage initial action
                    being taken by SAG and possibility untoward
                    action [by] Iran”. The Ambassador was given copies of draft decrees representing
                    the latest versions of ARAMCO annexes 2 and 3
                    as set forth in airgram 23, March 2, to Jidda, <ref target="#pg111">p. 111</ref>
                    (telegram 357, May 21, 5 p. m., from Jidda, 890.0145/5–2149).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
